1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
This is Neural Path Finder — Google Maps
for a fruit fly’s wiring.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
You play a fruit fly’s day
on a connectome map.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Tap a moment: tasting food, watching
a flickering screen, getting zapped.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
A cartoon path hops from sensors
toward movement cells.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000
It is a map of connections — not
a movie of the fly’s feelings.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Paths do not prove the fly thought,
decided, or felt that way.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
This is not medical advice.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The data is not a live lab feed.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The browser never talks to Janelia
at runtime.

10
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
A hand-authored file, connectome.json,
is written by generate_connectome.py

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
and loaded once into a NetworkX
directed graph.

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The published Male CNS has about 166,000
neurons and 125 million synapses.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
This app uses 75 neurons and 149 connections —
a compact teaching subgraph.

14
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Every edge is structural connectivity:
anatomy only.

15
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Here is what you can do on the live site.

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Eight scene cards: Taste Food, Watch TV,
Zapped By Human,

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Hot Sensation, Cold Sensation,
Smell Something Yummy,

18
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Hear a Buzz, and Smell Something Bad.

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,000
One tap runs a real pathfinder and returns
a short story plus ranked routes.

20
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The wide button asks: taste food versus
watch TV — do they meet?

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Scientist mode: search by ID, name, type,
region, or category. Classic demo: R1 → DNg13.

22
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Watch this on the live Azure app.

23
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
I tap Watch TV — photoreceptor R1
toward descending neuron DNg13.

24
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Status says: Following the wires.

25
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Story beats land first: the fly stares
at a glowing, flickering screen.

26
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Then the hop strip: R1, L1, Tm3,
LC10, AVLP713m, DNg13.

27
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Five hops. Synapse counts sit on the
tracks between stations.

28
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Most direct is selected. Strongest
connectivity and alternatives are other tabs.

29
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:14,000
I tap R1 to open branches — cells
before and after this station.

30
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Switch to Strongest connectivity to see
a bottleneck-aware ranking.

31
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Now Zapped By Human: bristle mechanoreceptor
toward giant-fiber-class DNp01.

32
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Same engine, different mood — a short
structural escape-style walk.

33
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Taste food versus watch TV —
do they meet?

34
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Two queries at once. Shared cells are meeting
points in the graph, not proof they co-occur.

35
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Scientist mode. Classic demo: R1 → DNg13.
You pick the endpoints.

36
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Architecture lives in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
on GitHub.

37
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:14,000
FastAPI serves the built Vite SPA and /api
from the same origin.

38
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Uvicorn on port 8000. connectome.json on disk.
No Janelia client at runtime.

39
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:30,000
graph.py builds a NetworkX DiGraph.
pathfinder.py ranks routes.

40
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Most direct is 1 / hop count. Strongest is
a bottleneck-aware synapse score.

41
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Alternatives maximize Jaccard distance
so they do not clone the first path.

42
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Hubs mix degree and betweenness — local
to these 75 nodes, not a decision center.

43
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:00,000
That is Neural Path Finder: a wiring map
you can play, not a movie of a fly’s feelings.

44
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:08,000
The live app and the GitHub repo
are on screen. Thanks for watching.
